Several people pointed out that DVI files created by different
TeX implemenations should only differ due to differences in
floating point arithmetic. That is not true. DVI files created
by different true TeX implementations can be quite different
if the TeX implementations use different values for dvi_buf_size.
TeX implementations may even omit the `DVI file optimizer':

| @ Versions of \TeX\ intended for small computers might well choose to =
omit
| the ideas in the next few parts of this program, since it is not =
really
| necessary to optimize the \.{DVI} code by making use of the |w0|, =
|x0|,
| |y0|, and |z0| commands. [...]

                                                                -- =
tex.web

Eberhard Mattes (mattes@azu.informatik.uni-stuttgart.de)


